ATH_0012>\nAs the square is cartesian we get the two dotted arrows <MATH_0013>, <MATH_0014> making the\ndiagram commute. Since <MATH_0015> is universally injective we get <MATH_0016>.\nThis forces <MATH_0017> as <MATH_0018>\nis an fpqc covering, see\nProperties of Spaces, Proposition\n<REF_0003>.\nHence <MATH_0019> is universally injective as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e3c9c489578bd802633a9a31c91a146f20295026cfdd0188a3a76956256d6224", "unit_id": "tag:041R:proof"}
